SUMMARY: AiRTIFICIAL VISIONS: An Immersive Exhibition on Art\, AI\, and H
 uman Identity.
DESCRIPTION:The ICFF presents AiRTIFICIAL VISIONS: a groundbreaking immer
 sive exhibition exploring the intersection of human creativity\, artifici
 al intelligence\, and visual storytelling. Presented as part of the Lavaz
 za IncluCity Festival and hosted at Illuminarium Toronto\, the exhibition
  runs June 25–July 25\, 2026\, in The Distillery Historic District in Tor
 onto. Curated around "The Human Figure in the Digital Age\," it features 
 internationally recognized AI artists presenting immersive digital works 
 that explore identity\, memory\, transformation\, and the evolving relati
 onship between technology and human expression.\n\n\nHours: Tuesday–Frida
 y 5:00 PM – 10:00 PM | Saturday–Sunday 12:30 PM – 9:30 PM\n\n\nTickets: G
 A tickets starting at $22. Exhibition + tasting experience: $45. Free adm
 ission for Lavazza IncluCity ticket holders (with the purchase of a movie
  ticket) and TMU students (student card required).\n\n\nContact: info@icf
 f.ca mailto:info@icff.ca | 416-893-3966
CATEGORIES:AI,ICFF,AI-Art
